A||||5||mblackwell||Headlight motor||||1||
Z||000000||mblackwell||05-18-2001||08:00 PM||||When I turn off my headlights (even if I just have the parking lights on) the left headlight motor keeps running for a few seconds after the light is down.  Does this mean that something is going bad? If not, I can live with the minor annoyance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||05-18-2001||08:12 PM||||does it make a grinding noise when it keeps running after the headlight is down?  If so it will not be to long until it needs to be rebuilt with gears and switchs or replaced.<BR>kits are avail.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||05-18-2001||09:56 PM||||What year is it. As it does matter as to what it is going to need.||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||05-18-2001||10:10 PM||||what has happened is that the bumpers inside the gear have worn out - they will need to be rebuilt with the kit from Rodney Dickman ( retails for about $25 ) - or buy a complete unit for $220 without rebuilding - your call.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000004||mblackwell||05-19-2001||12:16 AM||||Its an 88.  There is no griding and it never has trouble going up or down.  The thing that seems weird to me is that it does it even when only the parking lights were on.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||05-19-2001||12:43 AM||||This is just the plastic bushings inside your motor wearing out.  You can get some new ones from Rodney that include detailed instructions.  They're only five bucks a side I believe.  The instructions save you enough time for them to be worth it.  Here's <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>Rodney's Retail Site</A>.  I just did this to both my headlights, they had the same symptoms as yours, and both of them quit working withing two weeks of the other.  After you open and close your headlight 5-10 more times, they not only have a hard time going down right, they stop going up <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I recommend you order Rodney's kit ASAP, and put them in both sides as soon as you get them.  Good luck.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
